title: Wittorf Affair
subtitle: A crisis in the USPD?
new-page: true
view-if: uspd_relation >= 30 and year = 1928 and month >= 8 and month <= 10
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: wittorf_affair_seen = 1
tags: event

= Wittorf Affair

Our spies and contacts amongst the communists have brought news of a scandal engulfing the USPD leadership. An associate of USPD Deputy Chairman Ernst Thälmann, a USPD official named John Wittorf, is accused of embezzling campaign funds, diverting thousands of Reichsmarks for personal use, and Thälmann is accused of covering up the affair. The party's central committee considers this charge serious.

The Spartacists in the USPD, fearing the rise in the party's Communist faction, are said to have leaked this information to aid them in the intra-party struggle. Dissident communists in the Leninbund also have information about this affair, and are planning to publish it.

What should we do with this information?

- @publicize
- @nothing
- @weaponize

@publicize
title: We will publicize the scandal to damage the Communists and help the Spartacists, even at the cost of public damage to the USPD.
on-arrival: wittorf_secret = 1; uspd_relation -= 5; workers_uspd -= 3; unemployed_uspd -= 3

Our newspapers are among the first to publicize the affair, bringing a torment of criticism to the hypocrisy of the communists. We have damaged Thälmann's standing within the USPD, at the cost of in turn damaging the USPD's standing among the workers.

In the end, Stalin's pressure helps to keep Thälmann from facing much in the way of consequences.

@nothing
title: Do nothing with the information.
on-arrival: workers_uspd -= 2; unemployed_uspd -= 2

The information spreads without our help, leading to some loss of USPD support among the workers.


@weaponize
title: We will weaponize the scandal to damage the Communists and Spartacists alike.
on-arrival: uspd_relation -= 10; workers_uspd -= 3; unemployed_uspd -= 3

Our newspapers are among the first to publicize the affair, bringing a torment of criticism to the hypocrisy of the communists. We have damaged Thälmann's standing within the USPD and the USPD's standing among the workers more widely, at the cost of our relations.

In the end, Stalin's pressure helps to keep Thälmann from facing much in the way of consequences.
